#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:-1
msgid ""
"Learn how to configure and customize module file generation in Spack for "
"Environment Modules and Lmod."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:19
msgid "Modules (modules.yaml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:21
msgid ""
"The use of module systems to manage user environments in a controlled way is "
"a common practice at HPC centers that is sometimes embraced also by "
"individual programmers on their development machines. To support this common "
"practice Spack integrates with `Environment Modules <http://modules."
"sourceforge.net/>`_ and `Lmod <http://lmod.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`_ by "
"providing post-install hooks that generate module files and commands to "
"manipulate them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:24
msgid ""
"Modules are one of the several ways you can use installed packages, along "
"with :ref:`spack load <spack-load>` and :ref:`environments <environments>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:27
msgid "Quick start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:29
msgid ""
"Spack can generate both Tcl and Lua module files, either with a post-install "
"hook or at user's request through a command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:31
msgid ""
"If you're using the default configuration values, you can start by "
"generating Tcl module files for all currently installed packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:33
msgid "$ spack module tcl refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:37
msgid ""
"To generate Lua module files simply use the ``spack module lmod`` command "
"instead of ``spack module tcl``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:39
msgid ""
"Once module files are in place, add the Tcl module directory generated above "
"to your module path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../module_file_support.rst:41
msgid "$ module use $SPACK_ROOT/share/spack/modules/$(spack arch)"
msgstr ""

